hell:
n. any place of pain and turmoil;
n. a cause of difficulty and suffering
n. (Christianity) the abode of Satan and the forces of evil; where sinners suffer eternal punishment

hemlock:
n. poisonous drug derived from an Eurasian plant of the genus Conium
n. large branching biennial herb native to Eurasia and Africa and adventive in North America having large fernlike leaves and white flowers;
n. soft coarse splintery wood of a hemlock tree especially the western hemlock
